Debian packaging staging area for disgrace (targets Debian 13/trixie)
============================================================================

This directory mirrors the content of the `debian/` directory of a
non-native source package using the 3.0 (quilt) format. To build:

1. Produce the upstream tarball and use it as the .orig tarball:

       make dist
       cp disgrace-0.1.0.tar.gz ../disgrace_0.1.0.orig.tar.gz
       tar xzf disgrace-0.1.0.tar.gz
       cd disgrace-0.1.0

2. Copy this directory into place and build:

       cp -R /path/to/dist/debian debian
       dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

   (or `debuild -us -uc`). The build needs the Build-Depends from
   `control` installed; `sbuild`/`pbuilder`/`cowbuilder` handle that
   automatically.

Notes:

- The man page (`disgrace.1`) is installed via debhelper's automatic
  manpage handling.
- Festival and Piper TTS support auto-detects at configure time and
  stays off in a clean build environment, since those development
  packages are intentionally not in Build-Depends.
